# idtomask

- Label: ID to Mask
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 2
- Parameters: 26 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/idtomask.html
- Summary (EN): Creates a mask from an ID layer by selecting which IDs are included, to isolate regions for post-processing.
- Résumé (FR) : Crée un masque à partir d'une couche d'identifiants, en retenant les IDs par motif, plage, probabilité ou masque.

- Inputs meaning: ["id: the original ID layer to convert", "mask: optional per-pixel mask amount, scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "ID Pattern", "meaning": "group pattern selecting IDs; blank means all IDs"}, {"name": "Invert Mask", "meaning": "inverts the generated mask"}, {"name": "Keep by Range", "meaning": "selects IDs by Start and End, or Start and Length, with optional Range Offset; a Range Filter picks an alternating subset"}, {"name": "Keep by Chance", "meaning": "keeps IDs randomly by Probability (default 0.5); Seed (default 30) changes the pattern"}, {"name": "Keep within Mask", "meaning": "uses the mask input; Threshold (default 0.5) sets the minimum mask value considered"}]

- Caveats: ["Start ID and End ID apply only when their toggles are on.", "Keep within Mask needs a connected mask input to have any effect.", "The page does not document what the Mask parameter is."]

